Carafe bench: surface stores with a channel mask and surface load and store cache hints. NVK uploads
images with 1 and 2 byte texels through the compute shader vk-meta-copy-buffer-to-image-compute, which NAK
compiles to sust.p.r; Eden threw "Non-full mask", the pipeline was not built and the texture stayed empty,
including DXVK's HUD font (R8) and D3D9 L8 and R5G6B5 textures. A masked store now takes the enabled
channels from consecutive registers and writes zero to the others, as the hardware ignores them for the
format. Cache hints only change caching on the hardware, so SULD and SUST no longer reject them; NAK emits
other hints in descriptor-buffer shaders ("Cache 2").
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.
diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/maxwell/translate/impl/surface_load_store.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/maxwell/translate/impl/surface_load_store.cpp
